{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbYrM6xZS8WGCoUo1Kjw", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Flags here are a simple file-based system. The project memory says the same thing, and I checked it against the code: it matches.\n\n**How it works**\n- You declare each flag in `flags.toml` at the repo root, under `[flags]`, with a boolean default:\n  ```toml\n  [flags]\n  invoice-pdf-v2 = false\n  ```\n- You read flags only through `flags.is_on(\"name\")` from `src/flags.py`. There's also `flags.all_flags()` if you need all of them as a dict.\n- Flag names are kebab-case.\n\n**For your checkout flow**\n1. Add the flag to `flags.toml`:\n   ```toml\n   new-checkout-flow = false\n   ```\n2. Check it where the flows split:\n   ```python\n   from src import flags  # match however the module is imported elsewhere\n\n   if flags.is_on(\"new-checkout-flow\"):\n       return new_checkout(...)\n   return legacy_checkout(...)\n   ```\n\n**Things to watch for**\n- **Typos fail silently.** `is_on` calls `_FLAGS.get(name, False)` (`src/flags.py:8`), so a misspelled or undeclared name returns `False` with no error. Copy the name exactly from `flags.toml`.\n- **Changes need a restart.** `flags.toml` is read once when the module is imported (`src/flags.py:4`), so editing it doesn't affect a running process.\n- **No per-user or per-environment targeting.** Each flag is one global on/off value. If you want a gradual rollout or a toggle per environment, you'd have to extend `src/flags.py`.\n\nDo you want me to add the flag and wire it into the checkout code?"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 430, "cache_read_input_tokens": 21584, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 430}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, 